    "body": "The 14:45 UTC qualification trigger had no observed scheduled run by 15:21 while workflow 374465172 was active. Record that absence as MISSED_SCHEDULE, explicitly marking its 20-minute threshold as retrospective. A genuine scheduled FRESH run later appeared at 15:26:37 and passed on merged #11: https://github.com/ryansctt1994-sudo/introspection-twin/actions/runs/41857790032 . This does not erase the missed window; the original workflow did not retain the exact triggering cron.\n\nDaily FRESH replay now runs at 15:47 UTC. Commit prospective arrival (16:07 UTC) and completion (16:27 UTC) deadlines, a 16:29 UTC GitHub watchdog, a standalone read-only checker, and trigger records in replay logs/artifacts. Remove both old cron entries, including the dated one. Missing, late, disabled, failed, and overdue runs produce findings; incomplete or ambiguous API observations are INCONCLUSIVE. Metadata success does not qualify kernel replay.\n\nMerged at 64b89a5dc73a42fd062370178ffb62bb4f028187 after hosted FRESH run https://github.com/ryansctt1994-sudo/introspection-twin/actions/runs/41858726516 passed on final source ace927123d9b4b8dc2f77eed536914f06e5e8512. Validation includes 17 liveness controls, existing replay/logger controls, 11 lineage fixtures, Actionlint 1.7.7 for both workflows, real checker diagnostics, and zero checker/logger exits.\n\nReplay Schedule Watch is enabled on a separate ChatGPT scheduler for 16:57 UTC daily, first execution still unobserved. It audits actual replay evidence, every elapsed slot, and the GitHub watchdog (arrival/completion deadlines 16:49/16:54), then reports to the owner. Separate schedulers remain under the same principal; neither independent witnessing nor guaranteed availability is claimed.\n\nPolicy and evidence: docs/evidence/SCHEDULE_LIVENESS_2026-11-04.md and docs/evidence/SCHEDULE_MISS_2026-11-04.json.",
